cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Does the adaptive-vs-SGD generalization gap survive seed noise at small scale? A reduced-scale reproduction of Wilson et al. (2017)"
message: "If you use this reproduction, please cite both this artifact and the original paper."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Naf
    email: nafeelahmad05@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  An independent, pre-registered reproduction of the CIFAR-10 learning-rate sensitivity
  experiment in Wilson et al. (2017), "The Marginal Value of Adaptive Gradient Methods in
  Machine Learning". 140 runs (the paper's exact learning-rate grids x 5 optimizers x 5 seeds)
  on a reduced-scale CNN. The paper's headline generalization gap between non-adaptive and
  adaptive methods does not reproduce and inverts within seed noise; three other claims,
  including the dominance of learning rate over optimizer choice, reproduce.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - optimization
  - learning rate
  - adaptive gradient methods
  - CIFAR-10
